        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0039",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The time zone that the scheduled maintenance window executions are based on, in Internet Assigned Numbers Authority (IANA) format. For example: “America/Los_Angeles”, “UTC”, or “Asia/Seoul”. For more information, see the [[p0]] on the IANA website.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "Time Zone Database"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0040",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]] (integer)",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--schedule-offset"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0041",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The number of days to wait after the date and time specified by a cron expression before running the maintenance window.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0042",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "For example, the following cron expression schedules a maintenance window to run the third Tuesday of every month at 11:30 PM.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0043",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "cron(30 23 ? * TUE#3 *)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0044",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "If the schedule offset is [[p0]] , the maintenance window won’t run until two days later.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
